    "result_text": "The full suite is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned the owner `customerCode` from the old `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` sequence-based form to the new sequence-free `<REGION>-<HASH8>` identity, and moved every value derived from it onto that new identity.\n\n### `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`\n- Replaced `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` (and its per-city sequence lookup) with `customerCode(owner)`, which builds `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n  - **REGION** via a new `deriveRegion(postcode, city)` \u2014 postcode range match first (NSW/VIC/QLD), then the `CITY_REGION` table, then `UNKNOWN`.\n  - **HASH8** via `sha256HexUpper(telephone + lastName, 8)` \u2014 the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over the normalized telephone concatenated with the last name.\n- Added `java.security.MessageDigest`, `NoSuchAlgorithmException`, and `StandardCharsets` imports; updated the assignment comment. (`countOwnersInCity` is retained \u2014 still used by the city-capacity check.)\n\n### `OwnerMapper.java`\n- `locality(owner)` now reads the **REGION** segment out of the `<REGION>-<HASH8>` customer code (falling back to `UNKNOWN` for owners with no code, e.g. seed data), rather than independently re-deriving from postcode/city \u2014 so locality follows the frozen creation-time identity.\n- Removed the now-unused `REGION_POSTCODE_RANGES` map and `regionForPostcode` helper.\n- `checkDigit` (Luhn over the digits in the code) and `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`) automatically flow from the new code with no logic changes; updated their doc examples. The create audit line already logs `owner.getCustomerCode()`, so it now emits the region-and-hash code.\n\n### `openapi.yml`\n- Updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` field descriptions/examples to match the new identity.\n\nThe audit output during the test confirms the new form: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`, and the acceptance test (`customerCode` matches `[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}`) plus the full suite pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
